[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SUM001
TITLE: Start, stop, and edit runway designations for one airport
STATEMENT: >>>
The operator manual shall tell an operator how to edit runway designations in the airport TOML file, start the n local computers, and stop them. It shall state that a closed runway will not be assigned and that a file outside the checked envelope will not start. Acceptance is a manual section that names the TOML keys for designation and the start and stop commands, and an operator who can close a runway by editing the file and restarting.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The user of this CSCI is the airport operator who maintains the TOML file, not a pilot.
<<<
DAL: C
REQUIREMENT_LEVEL: Plan
VERIFICATION: Review
ASSUMPTIONS: The manual does not restate FAA JO 7110.65.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SDP001
